  {
   "text": "Five Tarkir: Dragonstorm Commander decks are released together with Tarkir: Dragonstorm on April 11, 2025.",
   "scene": 0,
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Each deck introduces 10 never-before-seen Commander cards to Magic: The Gathering . These consist of two borderless traditional foil mythic rare creatures and eight rare new-to- Magic cards in the default card frame . Non-foil borderless mythic rare creatures and extended-art new-to- Magic rare cards can be found in Collector Boosters .",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "New Dragonstorm Commander cards with the TDC set code numbered #1-50 (and their extended art versions numbered #51-90) are permitted in the Commander, Legacy, and Vintage formats. Returning cards with the TDC set code and numbered #91-413 are legal for play in any format where a card with the same name is permitted.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Multiple reprints in the Commander decks have new art (#91-107), almost all suited to the Dragonstorm theme. The one exception is Shadow Summoning , which is set on Innistrad .",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Each package contains:",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "2 foil Commanders (a clan leader and a spirit dragon). You can play with either and the decks work with both.",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "10 double-sided tokens",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "1 Collector Booster Sample Pack (2 cards)",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "For the digital release of Alchemy: Tarkir on Magic: The Gathering Arena , the ten face and reserve commanders ( Betor, Ancestor's Voice ; Elsha, Threefold Master ; Eshki, Temur's Roar ; Felothar the Steadfast ; Kotis, Sibsig Champion ; Neriv, Crackling Vanguard ; Shiko and Narset, Unified ; Teval, the Balanced Scale ; Ureni of the Unwritten ; Zurgo Stormrender ) were made available for players to craft. They are legal in Brawl , Historic , and Timeless .",
   "scene": 3,
   "section": "Magic: The Gathering Arena"
  },
  {
   "text": "A deck focusing on defenders that can turn toughness into power .",
